\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Exact finite action of a diagonal operator plus one thin correction. The bars display the same action as the explicit matrix.}}{2}{figure.caption.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The finite candidate tree has three prunings. The middle point is optimal under error budget four, although no nonnegative Lagrangian multiplier selects it.}}{3}{figure.caption.2}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The shaded region satisfies the supplied error budget. AFF is the unique minimum-cost assignment in that region. The model protects the first edge before spending on less sensitive edges.}}{4}{figure.caption.3}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The representation and the output contract are fixed before the device schedule is chosen.}}{6}{figure.caption.4}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces A packet intermediate representation stores active block addresses together with dimensions, block types, tolerances, and scheduling metadata.}}{8}{figure.caption.7}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces The ideal reduction grows with dimension only when packet width and transfer rank remain controlled.}}{12}{figure.caption.20}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces A representation can move the same mathematical problem between memory limited and compute limited regimes.}}{13}{figure.caption.25}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces A regular diagonal packet structure is coupled by global low rank factors.}}{17}{figure.caption.44}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces The approximation decision is made from the singular values of a small core whose dimension is the unrecompressed rank.}}{20}{figure.caption.55}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Composition creates possible support along directed paths. Cancellation can remove an allowed block, so the graph gives an inclusion rather than an equality.}}{22}{figure.caption.66}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Packets in the same topological level can be processed concurrently in a triangular solve.}}{23}{figure.caption.71}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces The block diagonal packet operator serves as a reusable local preconditioner in a weakly coupled positive system.}}{26}{figure.caption.82}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces More sensitive packet edges receive tighter continuous tolerances.}}{29}{figure.caption.93}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces The thick leaves are selected by the exact Lagrangian recurrence.}}{32}{figure.caption.100}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces The quantized dynamic program produces the exact cost and error frontier for its finite model.}}{34}{figure.caption.111}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {16}{\ignorespaces The corpus records timing scope and output contract as separate fields.}}{37}{figure.caption.128}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {17}{\ignorespaces Recorded device resident dense throughput across dimensions and scalar types.}}{38}{figure.caption.131}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {18}{\ignorespaces The speed and error tradeoff depends on both precision and problem size.}}{39}{figure.caption.132}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {19}{\ignorespaces Regular equal shapes expose both representation reduction and batched execution.}}{40}{figure.caption.133}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {20}{\ignorespaces Representation and launch strategy both affect BDLR application time.}}{41}{figure.caption.134}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {21}{\ignorespaces Compressed and explicit products answer different computational questions.}}{42}{figure.caption.135}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {22}{\ignorespaces A profitable repeated representation can remain unprofitable for one use.}}{43}{figure.caption.136}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {23}{\ignorespaces Device residence, transfer, graph replay, and a multioutput pipeline have different timing scopes.}}{44}{figure.caption.137}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {24}{\ignorespaces Values above one are slowdowns against the matched baseline.}}{45}{figure.caption.138}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {25}{\ignorespaces The best recorded gain differs strongly across suites. Regular packet structure dominates the largest measured rows.}}{45}{figure.caption.139}%
